\v 19 “Tell Aharon¦28353 to take¦28354 his staff¦28355 and¦28356 stretch¦28356 out¦28356 his hand¦28358 over¦28359 the¦28361 waters¦28361 of¦28361 Egypt¦28362: over¦28363 their streams¦28365, their¦28365 canals¦28369, and¦28370 their¦28372 pools¦28372, and¦28373 over¦28373 every¦28374 reservoir of their¦28377 water¦28377, and \add the water\add* will become¦28378 blood¦28380. Then¦28381 there'll be¦28381 blood¦28382 in¦28383 \add the entire country\add*—even in¦28387 wooden¦28387 or stone¦28388 containers \add of water\add*.”
