\v 15 \add By this time\add*, I¦29369 could have reached¦29369 out¦29369 and¦29373 struck¦29373 you¦29374 and¦29375 your¦29377 people¦29377 with¦29378 such \add ≈deadly disease¦29378 or destruction¦29379\add* that you¦29379 would all have been¦29379 obliterated from¦29380 the¦29382 land¦29382.
\v 16 However, I've¦29387 kept you¦29387 for this¦29386 reason¦29387: to¦29389 show¦29389 you¦29389 my¦29392 power¦29392 and¦29393 in order to¦29394 proclaim my¦29395 name¦29395 all¦29396 over the¦29398 world¦29398.\x + \xo 9:16: \xt Rom 9:17.\x*
\v 17 You're still¦29400 considering yourself¦29401 to be¦29401 greater than my¦29402 people¦29402 by failing to release them¦29404.
\v 18 \add Now\add* listen: I'm¦29406 about¦29407 to¦29407 cause extremely heavy¦29411 hail¦29410 to rain¦29407 \add down\add* at this time¦29408 tomorrow¦29409. \add It'll be hail like\add* which¦29413 has¦29416 never been¦29416 \add seen before\add* in¦29418 Egypt¦29418 from¦29419 the¦29421 day¦29421 it¦29422 was¦29422 founded¦29422 until now¦29425.
\v 19 \add ≈So¦29427\add* send¦29428 for your¦29432 livestock and¦29433 everything you own in¦29438 the¦29438 country now¦29427, and bring¦29429 it in under cover because¦29437 the¦29441 hail¦29452 will come¦29450 down¦29450 on¦29451 every person¦29441 and¦29442 animal¦29442 that¦29443 is¦29445 found¦29445 in¦29446 the countryside¦29446 and¦29447 not¦29447 \add sheltering under a roof\add*, and¦29453 they¦29453 will¦29453 die¦29453.’ ”
\v 20 Some of Far'oh's¦29461 servants¦29465 who believed what Yahweh¦29459 said, quickly brought their slaves and¦29466 their livestock¦29468 back into¦29469 their houses¦29471,
