\v 12 Then¦30004 Yahweh¦30005 told¦30004 Mosheh¦30008, “Extend¦30009 your¦30010 hand¦30010 over¦30011 Egypt¦30014 and let \add the locusts\add* rise up¦30016 over the¦30019 land¦30019, and¦30021 let \add them\add* devour¦30021 all¦30024 the¦30026 plants¦30026—everything which¦30031 the¦30033 hail¦30033 had spared.”
\v 13 \add ≈So¦30035\add* Mosheh¦30036 stretched¦30035 his¦30039 staff¦30039 out¦30035 over¦30040 Egypt¦30043, and¦30044 Yahweh¦30044 sent an east wind over the land¦30048 all¦30049 that¦30052 day¦30051 and¦30053 all¦30053 night¦30055. Then morning¦30056 came, and¦30058 the¦30059 east¦30059 wind had brought¦30060 the¦30063 locusts¦30063.
\v 14 The¦30066 locusts¦30066 covered across all¦30068 the¦30070 land¦30070 of¦30070 Egypt¦30071 and¦30072 came to rest everywhere¦30073 within the¦30074 \add country's\add* borders¦30074. They were extremely numerous—never before¦30078 were¦30081 there so¦30082 many locusts¦30083, and¦30085 it'll¦30087 never be¦30087 \add repeated again\add*.\x + \xo 10:14-15: \xt Rev 9:2-3.\x*
