\v 26 you'll¦33389 gather¦33389 it¦33389 for six¦33387 days¦33388 \add each week\add*, but¦33390 on¦33390 the¦33391 Saturday, there won't¦33393 be¦33394 any.”
\p
\v 27 \add However,\add* some¦33402 people¦33404 did go¦33401 out¦33401 to¦33405 collect¦33405 it, but¦33406 they¦33407 couldn't find¦33407 any,
\v 28 and¦33410 Yahweh¦33411 said¦33410 to¦33412 Mosheh¦33414, “For how long will you¦33418 all keep refusing¦33418 to¦33419 obey my¦33420 commands¦33420 and¦33421 my¦33421 laws¦33421?
\v 29 Listen, Yahweh¦33426 has¦33427 given¦33427 you¦33428 the¦33429 Rest Day, so¦33432 on the Friday he¦33433 gives¦33434 you¦33435 food¦33438 for two¦33439 days¦33439. On the Saturday, everyone¦33442 should stay¦33440 where they are—there's no need for anyone¦33447 to go¦33446 outside¦33446 \add searching\add*.”
\v 30 \add ≈So¦33452\add* the¦33453 people¦33453 \add ^didn't work\add* on the Saturday.
\p
\v 31 The¦33458 Israelis¦33460 named¦33463 it ‘manna¦33464’ \add (which sounds like Hebrew ‘What is it?’)\add*. It was¦33468 white¦33468 like coriander¦33467 seed¦33466, and¦33469 it tasted¦33469 like¦33470 \add #wafers¦33470\add* with¦33471 honey¦33471.\x + \xo 16:31: \xt Num 11:7-8.\x*
\v 32 Then¦33473 Mosheh¦33474 said¦33473, “This¦33475 is¦33476 the¦33476 procedure that¦33477 Yahweh¦33479 has¦33478 commanded¦33478: Keep¦33483 a full measure of¦33480 it¦33482 for preservation for your¦33484 descendants¦33484 so¦33485 that¦33485 they¦33487 can see¦33487 the¦33490 food¦33490 which¦33491 I¦33492 fed¦33492 you¦33493 in¦33494 the wilderness¦33494, when¦33495 I¦33495 brought¦33495 you out¦33495 from¦33497 Egypt¦33498.”
\v 33 \add ≈So¦33500\add* Mosheh¦33501 said¦33500 to¦33502 Aharon¦33504, “Take¦33505 a¦33506 jar¦33506 and¦33508 fill it with the¦33511 full two litres of¦33511 manna¦33514.\x + \xo 16:33: \xt Heb 9:4.\x* Place¦33515 it¦33516 in¦33517 front¦33517 of¦33517 Yahweh¦33518 for preservation for your¦33520 descendants¦33520.”
\v 34 \add So\add* Aharon¦33529 \add prepared the jar and kept it\add* (and¦33528 would \add eventually\add* place¦33528 it¦33528 \add in the box\add* with the \add stone tablets\add*.)
\v 35 The¦33534 Israelis¦33535 ate¦33536 manna¦33539 for forty¦33540 years¦33541, until¦33542 they¦33544 \add eventually\add* \add ≈left the¦33551 wilderness\add* and came¦33555 to¦33556 the¦33558 \add #borders¦33558\add* of¦33558 the¦33559 region¦33559 of¦33559 Canaan¦33560.\x + \xo 16:35: \xt Josh 5:12.\x*
\v 36 (Two litres is called an ‘omer¦33562’ which is¦33563 a tenth¦33563 of¦33563 a ‘efah’.)
\c 17
\s1 Yahweh gives water from a rock
\rem /s1 Water From the Rock; Water from the Rock
\r (Num. 20:1-13)
\p
\v 1 Then¦33568 all¦33569 the Israelis¦33574 moved on from¦33575 Siyn in the¦33575 wilderness¦33575, travelling following Yahweh's¦33582 instructions. They¦33583 camped¦33583 at¦33584 Refidim¦33584 \add but\add* there¦33585 was¦33585 no water¦33586 for the people to¦33587 drink¦33587.\x + \xo 17:1-7: \xt Num 20:2-13.\x*
\v 2 \add ≈So¦33590\add* the¦33591 people¦33591 argued with¦33592 Mosheh¦33594 \add again\add*, saying¦33595, “Give¦33596 us¦33598 water¦33599 to drink¦33600!”
\p “Why¦33604 are¦33606 you¦33606 all quarrelling¦33606 with¦33607 me¦33607?” Mosheh \add ≈answered\add*. “Why¦33608 are¦33610 you¦33610 all testing¦33610 Yahweh¦33613?”
\p
\v 3 \add But\add* the people were¦33615 \add very\add* thirsty¦33615 there¦33616 and¦33619 \add *they\add* murmured¦33619 against Mosheh¦33623, \add so\add* he¦33624 \add demanded\add*, “Is this¦33626 why you¦33627 brought¦33627 us¦33627 out of Egypt¦33628? To¦33629 kill¦33629 me¦33630 and¦33631 my¦33633 sons¦33633 and¦33634 my¦33636 cattle¦33636 with thirst¦33637?” ???
\p
\v 4 Mosheh¦33640 cried¦33639 out¦33639 to¦33641 Yahweh¦33643, \add asking\add*, “What¦33645 should I¦33646 do¦33646 for \add ^these\add* people¦33647? \add ≈It won't take much more\add* and¦33651 they'll¦33651 \add ≈kill¦33651\add* me¦33651.”
\p
\v 5 “Walk on¦33658 ahead of¦33659 the¦33660 people¦33660,” Yahweh¦33654 told¦33653 Mosheh¦33657, “and¦33661 take¦33661 some¦33663 of¦33663 the¦33663 Israeli¦33664 elders¦33663 with you, and¦33665 your¦33665 staff¦33665—the one which¦33666 you¦33667 struck¦33667 the¦33671 river¦33671 with. Take¦33672 it in¦33673 your¦33673 hand¦33673 and¦33674 go¦33674.
\v 6 Watch me. I¦33676 will¦33677 stand¦33677 \add ≈in front¦33678 of you\add* there¦33679 on¦33681 the¦33683 rock¦33683 at¦33684 Horev¦33684 \add !(Mt¦33684. Sinai¦33684)\add*. Then¦33685 you¦33685 will¦33685 strike¦33685 the rock¦33686 and¦33687 \add #water¦33689\add* will¦33687 come¦33687 out¦33687 of it¦33688, and¦33690 the¦33691 people¦33691 will¦33690 drink¦33690.” \add So\add* Mosheh¦33694 did that while the¦33695 Israeli¦33697 elders¦33696 watched.
\p
\v 7 \add @Mosheh¦33699\add* named¦33700 that place¦33701 \add both\add* ‘Massah¦33702’ \add (which means ‘testing’)\add* and¦33703 ‘Meribah¦33703’ \add (which means ‘complaining’)\add*, because of the conflict among the Israelis¦33709 and¦33710 because¦33710 of how they¦33711 tested¦33711 Yahweh¦33714 by saying¦33715, ‘Is¦33717 Yahweh¦33717 among¦33718 us or¦33719 not¦33721?’
\s1 Mosheh's arms held high to defeat Amalek
