\p
\v 8 Then¦33724 the Amalek¦33725 \add army\add* came¦33724 and¦33726 attacked Yisrael¦33729 at¦33730 Refidim¦33730,
\v 9 and¦33732 Mosheh¦33733 instructed Yehoshua¦33736 \add !(Joshua¦33736)\add*, “Choose¦33737 men¦33740 for¦33739 us¦33739 and¦33741 go¦33741 out¦33741 and fight¦33742 with Amalek¦33743. Tomorrow¦33744 I'll¦33745 be¦33746 stationed on¦33747 top¦33749 of¦33749 the¦33750 hill¦33750 with the¦33751 staff¦33751 of¦33751 God in¦33753 my¦33753 hand¦33753.”
\v 10 \add ≈So¦33755\add* Yehoshua¦33756 \add prepared\add* to fight¦33762 Amalek¦33763 as¦33757 Mosheh had¦33758 told¦33758 him¦33760, and¦33764 Mosheh¦33764, Aharon¦33765, and¦33766 Hur¦33766 climbed up¦33767 to the¦33768 top¦33768 of¦33768 the¦33769 hill¦33769.
\v 11 And¦33771 so it¦33771 happened that¦33778 when Mosheh¦33774 raised¦33773 his¦33775 arm¦33775, then¦33776 Yisrael¦33777 would be winning, \add but\add* when¦33778 he¦33779 \add ≈lowered his¦33780 arm¦33780\add*, then¦33781 Amalek¦33782 would start winning.
\v 12 \add However,\add* Mosheh's¦33785 arms got tired, so¦33787 they¦33787 got¦33787 a¦33789 \add large\add* stone¦33789 and sat¦33792 him on¦33793 it, and¦33794 Aharon¦33794 and¦33795 Hur¦33795 stood on each side of¦33797 him holding up his¦33797 arms¦33803, and¦33802 holding him \add ≈steady¦33804\add* in that position until¦33805 the¦33808 sun¦33808 went¦33807 down¦33792.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦33810\add* \add this was how\add* Yehoshua¦33811 defeated¦33810 Amalek¦33814 and¦33815 his army with \add #their swords¦33820\add*.
\v 14 Then¦33823 Yahweh¦33824 told¦33823 Mosheh¦33827, “Write¦33828 this¦33829 event in¦33831 the book¦33831 and¦33832 \add ≈read it aloud to\add* Yehoshua¦33834, because¦33835 I¦33838 will¦33838 certainly blot out¦33838 the¦33841 memory¦33841 of¦33841 Amalek¦33842 from¦33843 \add ≈off the¦33844 earth\add*.”\x + \xo 17:14: \xt Deu 25:17-19; 1Sam 15:2-9.\x*
\v 15 Then¦33846 Mosheh¦33847 built¦33846 an¦33848 altar¦33848 and¦33849 he¦33849 named¦33850 it ‘Yahweh-nissi’ \add (which means ‘Yahweh is my banner’)\add*,
\v 16 saying¦33855, “Because¦33856 \add ≈they battled\add* against Yah's¦33862 throne¦33861, then¦33855 Yahweh¦33864 \add ≈will battle¦33863\add* against Amalek¦33865 \add ≈throughout the generations\add*.”
\c 18
