\v 25 If¦36287 you¦36291 loan¦36291 money¦36289 to¦36291 any my¦36294 people¦36294 \add >who are\add* poor¦36297, you mustn't act like¦36303 an \add impartial\add* creditor¦36303 to \add #them\add*—you¦36306 mustn't charge \add #them\add* interest¦36308.\x + \xo 22:25: \xt Lev 25:35-38; Deu 15:7-11; 23:19-20.\x*
\v 26 If¦36311 you actually¦36313 take the¦36315 your¦36316 neighbour's¦36316 \add ≈cloak¦36315\add* as a security, you¦36321 must¦36321 return¦36321 it¦36321 to¦36322 them by sunset,\x + \xo 22:26-27: \xt Deu 24:10-13.\x*
