\v 1 Then¦36902 \add @Yahweh¦36905\add* told¦36905 Mosheh¦36904, “Come¦36906 up¦36906 \add the mountain\add* to¦36907 \add *me¦36909\add*—you¦36910, Aharon¦36911, Nadab¦36912, Abihu¦36913 and¦36914 seventy¦36914 of¦36915 the¦36915 Israeli¦36916 elders¦36915, and¦36917 you¦36917 must¦36917 \add stay\add* at a¦36918 distance¦36918 to worship¦36917.
\v 2 Then¦36920 Mosheh¦36921 alone¦36922 must¦36920 approach¦36920 \add *me¦36925\add*, \add but\add* \add @the others\add* mustn't come near¦36928, and¦36929 \add also\add* the¦36929 people¦36929 mustn't come¦36931 up¦36931 with¦36932 him¦36932.”
\p
\v 3 \add ≈So¦36934\add* Mosheh¦36935 went¦36934 and¦36936 explained to¦36937 the people \add ≈everything that Yahweh¦36942 had said¦36953, including¦36943\add* all¦36944 the¦36946 regulations. Then¦36947 all¦36948 of¦36948 the¦36950 people¦36950 answered¦36953 \add ≈in unison\add*, “We'll¦36961 do everything that¦36957 Yahweh¦36960 has¦36959 \add ≈told¦36959 us to do¦36961\add*.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦36963\add* Mosheh¦36964 wrote¦36963 \add ≈down everything that Yahweh¦36969 had instructed\add*. Then¦36970 he¦36970 got up early¦36970 in¦36971 the morning¦36971 and¦36972 built¦36972 an¦36973 altar¦36973 at the bottom of the¦36975 mountain¦36975 and¦36976 \add set up\add* twelve \add stone\add* pillars¦36978 for¦36979 the¦36981 twelve tribes¦36981 of¦36981 Yisrael¦36982,
