\v 9 Then¦37050 Mosheh¦37051, Aharon¦37052, Nadab¦37053, Abihu¦37054, and¦37055 seventy¦37055 Israeli¦37057 elders¦37056 climbed up \add the mountain\add*
\v 10 and¦37059 they¦37059 saw¦37059 the¦37061 god¦37061 of¦37061 Yisrael¦37062. Under¦37063 his¦37064 feet¦37064 was something like¦37065 a tile made¦37065 of sapphire¦37067 that \add ≈looked so¦37068 pure that it was as¦37068 clear¦37070\add* as the sky¦37069.
\v 11 Those Israeli¦37076 leaders saw¦37080 God and¦37080 \add ≈yet they¦37080 weren't harmed by him.\add*. Then¦37084 they¦37084 ate¦37084 and¦37085 drank¦37085 \add together\add*.
\s1 Mosheh's long stay on Mt. Sinai
\rem /s1 Moses on Mount Sinai
\p
\v 12 Then¦37088 Yahweh¦37089 told¦37088 Mosheh¦37092, “Come¦37093 up¦37093 to¦37094 me¦37094 on the¦37095 mountain¦37095 and¦37096 \add wait\add* there¦37098, and I¦37099 will give¦37099 you some stone¦37104 slabs with the¦37105 rules and¦37106 regulations that¦37107 I¦37108 have¦37108 written¦37108 \add on them so you can\add* to¦37109 teach¦37109 them¦37109 \add <to the people\add*.”
