\v 5 and¦37250 red-dyed ram¦37251 skins¦37253, fine leather, and¦37255 acacia¦37256 timber¦37255.
\v 6 \add Also\add* lamp oil¦37258, spices¦37260 for¦37261 \add making\add* anointing¦37262 oil and¦37263 fragrant¦37264 incense¦37263,
\v 7 onyx¦37268 and¦37269 \add other\add* gemstones for¦37271 setting¦37270 into the apron¦37271 and¦37272 the breastplate¦37272.
\v 8 Then¦37274 they¦37274 should make¦37274 me¦37275 a¦37276 residence \add so\add* I¦37277 can live¦37277 \add in it\add* among¦37278 them¦37278,
\v 9 according¦37280 to¦37280 the \add #patterns\add* that¦37281 I'll¦37282 show¦37283 you¦37284 for the residence¦37287 and¦37288 for all¦37290 of¦37290 its¦37292 utensils¦37292. You¦37294 all must¦37294 make¦37294 \add ≈all of it exactly to plan\add*.
\s1 The box to hold the stone slabs
\rem /s1 Plans for the Ark; The Ark of the Covenant; The Covenant Box; The Ark
\r (Exo. 37:1-9)
\p
\v 10 They¦37297 must¦37297 make¦37297 a wooden chest¦37298 from acacia¦37300 wood¦37299. It should be¦37301 125cm long¦37303, with the width¦37306 and the height¦37309 being 75cm.
\v 11 It must¦37311 be overlaid¦37311 with pure¦37314 gold \add sheeting\add* on the outside¦37316 and the inside¦37315, and¦37318 have a¦37320 gold moulding¦37320 \add fitted\add* all¦37322 around¦37322 it.
\v 12 Four¦37326 gold¦37328 rings must be cast¦37324 and¦37329 attached to the¦37331 four¦37331 feet¦37332—two rings on each side.
\v 13 Make¦37346 two \add carrying\add* poles¦37347 from acacia¦37349 wood¦37348 and¦37350 overlay¦37350 them¦37351 with gold¦37352 \add sheeting\add*.
\v 14 Those poles¦37357 will¦37354 be inserted through¦37366 the¦37357 rings¦37358 on¦37359 the¦37360 sides¦37360 of¦37360 the¦37361 chest¦37361 so¦37354 it can be \add picked up and\add* carried¦37362 on them¦37366.
\v 15 The¦37371 poles¦37371 must be kept in¦37368 the¦37368 rings¦37368 on the¦37369 chest¦37369—they mustn't be¦37373 removed¦37373.
\v 16 The¦37381 \add ≈two stone slabs that¦37382 I'll¦37383 give¦37383 you¦37384 with our agreement inscribed on them\add* must be placed¦37376 inside the¦37379 chest¦37379.
\p
\v 17 You¦37386 must¦37386 make¦37386 a¦37391 lid the same length¦37392 and¦37393 width¦37395 as the chest. It must¦37393 be¦37393 made of¦37395 pure¦37389 gold¦37388 \add and will be known as\add* ‘the atonement¦37387 platform’.\x + \xo 25:17: \xt Heb 9:5.\x*
\v 18 Then¦37397 make¦37397 a pair of winged-creatures from gold¦37400 that's hammered¦37401 from¦37404 the¦37404 two¦37404 ends¦37405 of¦37405 the¦37406 atonement¦37406 platform.
\v 19 \add Yes,\add* make¦37408 one winged-creature from each end of the gold lid material.
\v 20 \add *Their\add* up-lifted wings¦37433 should spread¦37432 out¦37432 covering¦37435 the¦37439 atonement¦37439 platform and¦37440 they¦37448 should be¦37448 facing each¦37441 other across the¦37449 top of¦37449 the¦37450 platform.
\v 21 When¦37452 I¦37468 give¦37468 you¦37452 the \add stone\add* slabs, put¦37452 them inside the box and then fasten the¦37455 atonement¦37455 platform on¦37456 top to form the lid.
\v 22 Then¦37471 I'll¦37471 meet¦37471 with you there¦37473, and from¦37476 the¦37477 atonement¦37477 platform between¦37478 the¦37479 two¦37479 winged-creatures and above¦37482 the¦37484 \add stone\add* slabs, I'll¦37490 be able to tell¦37474 you¦37491 my commands¦37490 to pass on to the¦37494 Israelis¦37495.
\s1 The bread offering table
\rem /s1 The Table for the Bread of the Presence; Plans for the Table; The Table for the Bread Offered to God; The Table
\r (Exo. 37:10-16)
\p
\v 23 You¦37498 must¦37498 make¦37498 a¦37499 table¦37499 from acacia¦37501 wood¦37500: one metre long¦37503, 500cm wide¦37505, and 750cm high¦37508.
\v 24 Overlay¦37510 it¦37511 with pure¦37513 gold and¦37514 have a¦37516 gold moulding¦37516 fitted all¦37518 around¦37518 it.
\v 25 Make¦37520 an 8cm wide¦37523 rim¦37522 around¦37524 it and¦37525 fit a¦37526 gold¦37528 moulding¦37526 onto the rim¦37529.
\v 26 Make¦37532 four¦37534 gold¦37536 rings and¦37537 attach them near the¦37540 legs on¦37541 the¦37542 four¦37542 corners¦37543 \add of the table\add*
\v 27 near¦37548 the¦37549 rim¦37549. \add @The¦37550 rings¦37550\add* are¦37550 so poles¦37553 can be inserted in order to¦37554 carry¦37554 the¦37557 table¦37557.
\v 28 Make¦37559 \add two\add* poles¦37562 out of¦37563 acacia¦37564 wood¦37563 and¦37565 overlaid¦37565 them¦37566 with gold¦37567 for carrying¦37568 the¦37573 table¦37573.
\v 29 \add In addition,\add* make¦37575 the necessary plates¦37576 and¦37577 pans¦37577, and¦37578 the pitchers¦37578 and¦37579 bowls¦37579 to be¦37581 used for pouring¦37581 out¦37581 \add <the wine offerings\add*—all from pure¦37584 gold¦37583.
\v 30 You¦37588 must¦37588 keep \add sacred\add* bread¦37592 on¦37589 the¦37591 table¦37591 continually¦37595 in front¦37594 of me.\x + \xo 25:30: \xt Lev 24:5-8.\x*
\s1 The lampstand
\rem /s1 The Lampstand; Plans for the Lampstand
\r (Exo. 37:17-24)
\p
\v 31 You¦37598 must¦37598 make¦37598 a¦37599 lampstand¦37599 from pure¦37601 gold¦37600. The¦37604 base¦37605 and¦37606 shaft¦37606 are to be hammered¦37602 out \add of one piece of gold\add* as well as its¦37606 cups¦37607 and \add decorative\add* buds¦37608 and¦37609 flowers¦37609.
\v 32 There must¦37615 be¦37615 six¦37613 branches¦37619 extending from¦37621 the¦37622 shaft—three¦37623 on each side¦37626.
\v 33 Three cups shaped like almond flowers must be on each branch along with a bud and petals.
\v 34 The¦37651 \add centre\add* shaft must¦37651 have four¦37652 cups¦37653 like¦37654 almond¦37654 flowers¦37654 along with a bud and¦37656 petals.
\v 35 For each of¦37660 the¦37661 three pairs of branches¦37661 \add (one branch out each side in each pair)\add*, make a¦37663 bud \add on the centre shaft\add* so each pair of¦37665 branches¦37666 appear to be¦37669 growing out¦37676 of¦37671 it¦37673.
\v 36 These buds¦37681 and¦37682 their¦37682 branches¦37682 must¦37684 all¦37685 be¦37686 hammered¦37686 out from \add that\add* single¦37687 piece of pure¦37689 gold¦37688.
\v 37 Make¦37691 seven¦37695 lamps and¦37696 set them up¦37696 on it¦37700 to give¦37700 light¦37700 out from the¦37703 front¦37704 of¦37704 it,
\v 38 and¦37706 make all the utensils and¦37707 dishes for the lamps from pure¦37709 gold¦37708.
\v 39 This can all¦37717 be made¦37714 from 35kg of¦37717 pure¦37713 gold¦37712
\v 40 and be sure to make¦37723 it all like the pattern¦37724 that¦37725 you're¦37727 being¦37728 shown¦37728 on¦37729 the mountain¦37729.\x + \xo 25:40: \xt Acts 7:44; Heb 8:5.\x*
\c 26
\s1 Plans for the sacred residence
\rem /s1 Plans for the Tabernacle; The Tabernacle; The Tent of the Lord's Presence
\r (Exo. 36:8-38)
\p
\v 1 You¦37735 must¦37735 make¦37735 \add &my\add* residence with ten¦37736 fabric panels formed by a¦37746 skilled¦37746 craftsman. They must be made from twisted¦37739 finely-spun linen¦37738, with winged-creatures \add embroidered on them using\add* blue, purple¦37741, and¦37742 scarlet thread.
\v 2 The hanging panels must all¦37764 be the same size¦37762: 14.5m long¦37750 and two metres wide¦37757.
\v 3 Five¦37768 of¦37769 the¦37769 panels will¦37770 be¦37770 coupled together \add as one set\add* and¦37776 the other five¦37776 as another.
\v 4 For each set, make¦37784 loops¦37785 of¦37785 blue cloth and¦37793 fasten them along the outer¦37797 edge of each of the end¦37791 panels—
\v 5 place fifty loops on the¦37809 end¦37809 of¦37809 each set¦37812 so¦37806 that¦37811 the¦37813 loops¦37815 are¦37814 opposite¦37814 each¦37816 other.
\v 6 You'll¦37821 also need to make¦37821 fifty¦37822 gold¦37824 clips to join¦37825 the¦37829 two sets together to¦37831 make a single¦37837 walled structure.
\p
\v 7 You¦37840 must¦37840 make¦37840 eleven panels with goats¦37842' hair¦37842 to¦37843 form a¦37843 tent¦37843 over¦37844 the¦37846 residence¦37846.
\v 8 Each of the eleven panels must be the same size¦37865: 15m long¦37854 and¦37860 two metres wide¦37860.
\v 9 You¦37871 must¦37871 join¦37871 five¦37874 panels into a set, and¦37877 six¦37879 panels into the¦37880 other set so¦37882 that the¦37886 sixth¦37886 panel can be doubled¦37882 over at the¦37889 front¦37889 of¦37890 the¦37891 tent¦37891.
\v 10 You¦37893 must¦37893 make¦37893 50 loops¦37895 to go onto the¦37897 end of¦37897 one¦37899 set¦37901, and¦37902 another 50 for the¦37905 edge¦37905 of¦37905 the other set¦37907.
\v 11 You'll¦37910 also need to make¦37910 fifty¦37913 bronze¦37912 clips to join¦37919 the two sets together¦37919 to make the¦37922 tent¦37922 cover.
\v 12 Let the extra half¦37930 panel hang over¦37934 the¦37935 back of¦37936 the¦37936 residence¦37936.
\v 13 The half metre of extra length¦37943 on each side \add that extends beyond the linen sets\add* will¦37946 hang \add evenly\add* over¦37948 the¦37950 sides¦37950.
\p
\v 14 You¦37956 must¦37956 make¦37956 a¦37957 covering¦37957 of¦37959 rams¦37960 hides dyed¦37961 red¦37961 to go over the tent¦37958, then¦37962 another covering¦37962 sea-cow hides to¦37965 go over that.
\s2 The wooden frames
\rem /s1 The Framework
\p
\v 15 You¦37968 must¦37968 make¦37968 frames¦37971 for¦37972 \add &my\add* residence¦37972 from acacia¦37974 wood¦37973. They'll stand¦37975 upright¦37975
\v 16 \add and\add* each one¦37986 must¦37977 be¦37977 five metres¦37978 high and 0.75m wide¦37984.
\v 17 Each frame must have two¦37988 protrusions so¦37997 it can be connected to¦37990 the¦37990 frame¦37990 next to it.
\v 18 Assemble twenty¦38008 frames¦38009 for the¦38010 south side¦38010 of¦38010 the residence
\v 19 along with forty¦38014 silver¦38017 bases to go underneath¦38019 them—two¦38022 bases¦38023 supporting each frame¦38026, and¦38030 each frame having two protrusions at the bottom to go into the bases.
\v 20 For¦38039 the¦38043 north¦38043 side, assemble twenty¦38044 frames¦38045
\v 21 along with forty¦38047 silver¦38049 bases¦38051—two¦38055 under¦38057 each frame¦38058.
\v 22 For¦38061 the¦38061 rear of¦38061 the¦38062 residence¦38062 facing west¦38063, assemble six¦38065 frames¦38066
\v 23 plus¦38068 two¦38068 extra frames¦38069 for¦38071 \add bracing\add* the¦38071 two back corners¦38071—
\v 24 they must be joined \add on\add* at the bottom and then both¦38090 of¦38090 them¦38090 have their tops attached to¦38091 a ring¦38086.
\v 25 Then¦38095 assemble eight¦38096 frames¦38097 with their¦38098 sixteen silver¦38099 bases—two bases supporting each frame.
\p
\v 26 Make¦38114 crossbars¦38115 from acacia¦38117 wood¦38116—five¦38118 of them to¦38119 go across the¦38119 frames¦38119 on the¦38120 northern side¦38120,
\v 27 five¦38125 for the south side¦38128, and¦38132 five¦38132 for the¦38134 frames¦38134 at the¦38135 rear of¦38135 the¦38136 residence¦38136 on¦38138 the western¦38138 side.
\v 28 The¦38141 middle¦38141 crossbar in¦38142 the¦38142 centre¦38142 of¦38143 the¦38143 frames¦38143 will¦38144 go¦38144 right through¦38144 from¦38145 one end¦38147 to¦38148 the¦38150 other.
\v 29 Overlay the¦38154 frames¦38154 and the crossbars with gold¦38156, and¦38157 make¦38160 the rings¦38159 for¦38163 holding the¦38167 crossbars¦38167 with gold¦38168.
\v 30 Then¦38170 you¦38170 must¦38170 assemble¦38170 \add &my¦38173\add* residence¦38173 exactly as per the plan¦38174 that¦38175 you¦38176 were¦38176 shown¦38176 on¦38177 the mountain¦38177.
\s2 The curtain
\rem /s1 The Curtain
\p
\v 31 You¦38180 must¦38180 have a¦38189 skillful¦38189 workman make¦38180 a¦38181 curtain¦38181 from twisted¦38187 finely-spun linen¦38186, with winged-creatures \add embroidered on them using\add* blue, purple¦38183, and¦38184 scarlet thread.
\v 32 Hang it¦38195 from gold clips on¦38196 four¦38198 pillars¦38199 made from acacia¦38200 wood overlaid¦38201 with gold on¦38205 four¦38207 silver¦38210 bases¦38208.
\v 33 Hang the¦38215 curtain¦38215 under¦38216 the¦38217 clips, then¦38218 bring¦38218 the¦38223 box¦38223 that contains the agreement inside¦38220 the curtain. That curtain will¦38225 separate¦38225 for¦38227 you¦38227 between¦38228 the¦38229 sacred¦38229 section and¦38230 the \em very\em* sacred interior.\x + \xo 26:33: \xt Heb 6:19; 9:3-5.\x*
\v 34 Install the¦38237 atonement¦38237 platform as the lid on¦38238 the¦38239 box¦38239 there in¦38241 the very sacred interior.
\v 35 Set¦38244 the¦38247 table¦38247 up outside¦38248 the curtain¦38249 on¦38255 the¦38256 north¦38264 side¦38256, with the¦38252 lampstand¦38252 on¦38261 the¦38263 south¦38258 side¦38263 opposite¦38253 the table.
\p
\v 36 Then¦38266 make¦38266 a¦38267 curtain out of twisted¦38275 finely-spun linen¦38274 for¦38268 the¦38268 entrance¦38268 of¦38268 the¦38269 tent¦38269. It should be embroidered with blue, purple¦38271 and¦38272 scarlet yarn.
\v 37 Make¦38279 five¦38281 pillars¦38282 for the curtain from acacia¦38283 wood overlaid¦38284 with gold¦38286. The hooks¦38287 on them must¦38288 be¦38288 made of gold¦38288, and¦38289 their five¦38291 bases¦38292 must be cast¦38289 with bronze¦38293.
\c 27
\s1 The altar for burnt offerings
\rem /s1 Plans for the Altar of Burnt Offering; The Altar of Burnt Offering; The Altar
\r (Exo. 38:1-7)
\p
\v 1 Make¦38296 an altar¦38299 from acacia¦38301 wood¦38300 that's 2.5m square¦38308 and¦38311 1.5m high¦38313
\v 2 and¦38315 as part of that same piece of wood, include \add a carved projection like\add* a horn on¦38317 each of the¦38318 top corners¦38319 of¦38319 the altar. Overlay¦38323 \add @the¦38324 altar¦38324\add* with bronze¦38325.
\v 3 Make¦38327 pots¦38328 for the ashes¦38329 out of¦38336 bronze¦38338, along with the necessary shovels¦38330, sprinkling bowls¦38331, meat forks¦38332, and¦38333 fire-trays¦38333.
\v 4 Then¦38340 make¦38340 a¦38342 bronze grating¦38342 for it with four¦38350 rings¦38351 of¦38351 bronze¦38352 on¦38353 the four¦38354 corners.
\v 5 Fit it¦38358 down onto a ledge¦38360 inside the¦38361 altar¦38361 so¦38363 that it¦38363 sits inside the¦38367 altar¦38367 about halfway¦38366 up.
\v 6 \add Also,\add* make¦38369 poles¦38370 from acacia¦38374 wood¦38373 for¦38371 the altar¦38371 and¦38375 overlay¦38375 them¦38376 with bronze¦38377.
\v 7 They'll¦38384 be able to be¦38379 put¦38379 into¦38383 rings¦38383 on¦38386 two¦38388 sides¦38389 of¦38389 the¦38390 altar¦38390 for carrying¦38391 it¦38392.
\v 8 The altar should be hollow¦38394 in the middle and made¦38396 from \add wooden\add* planks just¦38398 like¦38398 you¦38400 were shown¦38399 on¦38401 the mountain¦38401.
\s1 The courtyard around the sacred tent
\rem /s1 Plans for the Courtyard; The Enclosure for the Tent of the Lord's Presence; The Courtyard; The Court and Its Hangings
\r (Exo. 38:9-20)
\p
\v 9 Make¦38406 curtains¦38414 of twisted¦38417 finely-spun linen¦38416 \add to form\add* a courtyard \add around\add* the¦38409 residence¦38409. The¦38411 south¦38411 side will¦38418 require fifty metres of¦38421 \add ≡curtain\add*
\v 10 with twenty \add bronze\add* pillars and¦38426 their¦38426 twenty¦38427 bases¦38426. The¦38429 hooks¦38429 on the¦38430 pillars¦38430 and¦38431 the clips must¦38432 be¦38432 made of silver¦38432.
\v 11 Similarly on the¦38435 north¦38436 side¦38435, \add another\add* fifty metres of¦38435 \add #curtain¦38438\add* with twenty¦38443 pillars¦38448 and¦38444 their bases¦38444 and their¦38444 hooks¦38447 and¦38449 clips.
\v 12 The¦38456 west¦38456 side¦38454 will require twenty-five metres of¦38454 \add #curtain¦38457\add* with ten pillars¦38460 and¦38462 bases¦38462.
\v 13 The¦38465 east side¦38467 of¦38465 the¦38466 courtyard¦38466 must¦38470 also¦38465 be¦38470 twenty-five metres wide¦38465.
\v 14 Only side side of the gate, the curtain¦38476 will¦38479 be¦38479 7.5m long with three¦38479 pillars¦38478 and¦38480 bases¦38480,
\v 15 and¦38483 the same on the other side¦38483.
\v 16 The¦38494 entrance¦38494 curtain must be made¦38506 of twisted¦38505 finely-spun linen¦38504. It'll be ten metres wide and hang on four pillars¦38508 with their¦38508 bases¦38510, and must be embroidered with blue, purple¦38501, and¦38502 scarlet yarn.
\v 17 All¦38513 the¦38515 pillars¦38515 for the¦38516 courtyard¦38516 must¦38518 have silver¦38519 decorations around¦38517 them, as well as their¦38520 silver¦38521 hooks¦38520 and¦38522 bronze¦38523 bases¦38522.
\v 18 \add So\add* the¦38526 courtyard¦38526 will¦38527 be¦38527 fifty metres by¦38528 twenty-five metres and¦38529 the¦38529 curtain enclosure will¦38531 be¦38531 2.5m high¦38533. All the¦38533 curtains will¦38534 be¦38534 made of finely-spun linen¦38536, and¦38538 the bases¦38538 under all the pillars will¦38539 be¦38539 bronze¦38539.
\v 19 All¦38541 the¦38542 equipment¦38542 for the operation of¦38542 the¦38543 residence¦38543 and all the tent pegs and pegs for the¦38552 courtyard¦38552 must¦38553 be¦38553 made of bronze¦38553.
\s1 The oil for the lamps
\rem /s1 Oil for the Lampstand; The Oil for the Lamp; Taking Care of the Lamp
\r (Lev. 24:1-4)
\p
\v 20 Order the¦38561 Israelis¦38562 to bring¦38563 you¦38564 pure¦38567, pressed¦38568 olive¦38566 oil¦38565 for¦38569 the \add #lamps¦38571\add* so they can be kept burning continually¦38572.
\v 21 In¦38574 the¦38574 outer portion of¦38574 the¦38576 \add sacred\add* tent¦38574 (outside¦38576 the curtain¦38577 where the \add sacred\add* box is¦38579 kept), Aharon¦38584 and¦38585 his¦38585 sons¦38585 must¦38582 attend to¦38590 the¦38590 lampstand in¦38590 front¦38590 of¦38590 Yahweh¦38591 from¦38586 evening¦38586 to morning¦38589. This regulation¦38592 will¦38594 apply continually to¦38594 all future generations¦38594 of¦38596 Israelis¦38597.
\c 28
\s1 The priests' uniform
\rem /s1 Vestments for the Priesthood; The Priestly Garments; Garments for the Priests; Clothing for the Priests
\r (Exo. 39:1-7)
\p
\v 1 \add Now,\add* have your¦38606 brother¦38606 Aharon and¦38607 his sons brought¦38601 to¦38602 you from¦38611 among¦38611 the¦38612 Israelis¦38613. Aharon¦38617, Nadab¦38618, Abihu¦38619, Eleazar¦38620, and¦38621 Ithamar¦38621 will become my priests¦38614.
\v 2 Make¦38625 \add ≈sacred¦38628\add* clothes¦38626 for¦38629 Aharon¦38629—they must be \add uniquely\add* beautiful¦38632
\v 3 \add ≈so¦38634\add* speak¦38635 to¦38636 all¦38638 the \add ≈skilled¦38640 craftsmen who've been given\add* the spirit¦38645 of¦38645 wisdom¦38646, and¦38647 they¦38647 can make¦38647 Aharon's¦38651 clothes¦38650 to¦38652 \add ≈dedicate¦38652 him¦38652 as¦38653\add* my priest¦38653.
\v 4 These¦38657 are¦38658 the¦38658 clothes¦38658 that¦38659 they'll¦38660 need to make¦38660: a¦38661 small pouch to hang around the neck and¦38662 an¦38662 apron¦38662, a¦38663 robe¦38663 and¦38664 a¦38664 tunic¦38664 of¦38664 woven work¦38665, and a¦38666 turban¦38666 and¦38667 a¦38667 waistband¦38667. They¦38668 must¦38668 make¦38668 \add those\add* \add ≈sacred¦38671\add* clothes for¦38672 your¦38673 brother¦38673 Aharon¦38672 and¦38674 for¦38674 his¦38674 sons¦38674 to¦38675 serve¦38675 as¦38675 my priests¦38675.
\v 5 \add @The skilled craftsmen\add* must¦38680 \add ≈be given\add* gold¦38683 \add wire\add* and blue, purple¦38689, and¦38690 scarlet yarn, and¦38694 finely-spun linen¦38696.
\rem /s1 The Ephod; Design of the Ephod
\p
\v 6 They¦38699 must¦38699 make¦38699 the¦38702 sacred apron¦38702 from twisted¦38709 finely-spun linen¦38708 with gold¦38703 \add wire\add* and¦38705 blue, purple¦38705, scarlet yarn embroidered onto it by a¦38711 skilled¦38711 craftsman.
\v 7 It should have two shoulder pieces attached to¦38719 \add the top\add* two¦38721 corners so¦38723 it¦38723 can be¦38723 fastened.
\v 8 Then¦38725 the¦38725 waistband¦38725 for the apron¦38726 shall be¦38729 made with similar¦38729 workmanship¦38729 from¦38730 twisted¦38738 finely-spun linen¦38737 with gold¦38732 \add wire\add* and¦38734 blue, purple¦38734, and¦38735 scarlet yarn skillfully embroidered into it.
\v 9 Then¦38740 get¦38740 two¦38743 onyx¦38746 stones¦38744 and¦38747 engrave¦38747 the¦38749 names¦38749 of¦38749 Yisra'el's¦38751 \add twelve\add* sons¦38750 onto them—
\v 10 six¦38753 names¦38754 on¦38755 one¦38757 stone and¦38758 six¦38761 on¦38763 the other, in their¦38767 birth order.
\v 11 A stone¦38771 craftsman with experience at making¦38787 signet rings should do the¦38772 engravings¦38772, and then mount the¦38777 two¦38777 stones¦38778 in decorative gold¦38786 settings¦38785.
\v 12 Then¦38790 attach the¦38793 two¦38793 stones¦38794 to the¦38796 shoulder pieces of¦38796 the¦38797 apron¦38797 as a reminder¦38799 about¦38800 Yisra'el's¦38801 sons¦38800. That way Aharon¦38803 will¦38802 carry¦38802 their¦38806 names¦38806 on¦38809 his¦38812 two shoulders as a¦38813 reminder¦38813 \add every time\add* he goes to face¦38807 Yahweh¦38808.
\v 13 Make¦38816 the decorative settings¦38817 for the \add two\add* stones from gold¦38818,
\v 14 and¦38820 then make¦38825 two¦38820 twisted¦38824 chains¦38821 of¦38821 pure¦38823 gold¦38822 like a¦38827 cord that you¦38829 can attach to the decorative settings¦38836.
\s1 The chestpiece
\rem /s1 Design of the Chestpiece; The Breastpiece; The Breastplate
\r (Exo. 39:8-21)
\p
\v 15 Make¦38839 a¦38840 \bd \+add sacred\+add* chest pouch\bd* for \add ≈important decision¦38841 making\add*. A¦38843 skilled¦38843 craftsman should make¦38846 it¦38846 from twisted¦38853 finely-spun linen¦38852 like¦38844 the¦38844 apron¦38845, embroidered with gold¦38847 \add wire\add* and¦38849 blue, purple¦38849, and¦38850 scarlet yarn.
\v 16 It¦38858 needs to be¦38858 23cm square¦38857 when¦38862 folded¦38859 over double¦38859,
\v 17 and¦38865 it will have four¦38869 rows¦38870 of¦38872 \add three\add* gemstones on it: a¦38873 \add red\add* ruby¦38873, a¦38874 \add yellow\add* topaz¦38874, a¦38875 \add green\add* emerald,
\v 18 then¦38879 a¦38881 turquoise¦38881, a¦38882 \add blue\add* sapphire¦38882, a diamond,
\v 19 then¦38885 a¦38887 \add red\add* jacinth¦38887, a \add white\add* agate¦38888, a \add purple\add* amethyst¦38889,
\v 20 and¦38891 in the¦38891 last row¦38891, a¦38893 \add yellow\add* beryl, an¦38894 onyx¦38894, and¦38895 a¦38895 \add green\add* jasper¦38895. All those stones must¦38898 be¦38898 mounted in¦38899 decorative gold¦38897 settings¦38899,
\v 21 ⇔and \add so\add* they'll¦38902 represent the¦38905 twelve tribes¦38923 of Yisrael¦38908. The names of the twelve sons¦38906 must be engraved¦38914 on the¦38901 stones¦38901 similar to how signet rings \add are made\add*.
\v 22 Make¦38925 two twisted¦38930 chains¦38929 of¦38929 pure¦38934 gold¦38933 like a cord that you can attach to the pouch,
\v 23 then¦38936 make¦38936 two¦38940 gold¦38942 rings and attach them to the two \add top\add* corners of the pouch.
\v 24 Attach the¦38957 two¦38957 gold¦38959 chains to the¦38963 rings¦38963 on the corners
\v 25 with the other ends¦38971 fastened to the two decorative settings¦38978 \add around the stones\add* and¦38979 then attached to¦38984 the¦38986 front¦38986 side of the shoulder straps.
\v 26 Make¦38989 two¦38990 more gold¦38992 rings¦38991 and¦38993 attach them¦38994 on¦38995 the inside¦39008 to¦39004 the¦39006 two \add bottom\add* corners of¦39006 the¦39007 pouch,
