\r (Exo. 30:18)
\p
\v 8 Then¦44502 he¦44502 made¦44502 a bronze¦44505 washbasin and¦44506 base¦44507.\x + \xo 38:8: \xt Exo 30:18.\x* \add They were made\add* with¦44509 the bronze from the¦44509 mirrors¦44509 of¦44509 the¦44510 serving¦44510 women¦44510 who¦44511 served¦44512 at the¦44513 entrance¦44513 of¦44513 the¦44514 \add sacred\add* tent¦44514.
\s1 Making the courtyard
\rem /s1 Making the Court of the Tabernacle; The Enclosure for the Tent of the Lord's Presence; The Courtyard; Building the Courtyard
\r (Exo. 27:9-19)
\p
\v 9 Then¦44518 \add @Bezalel¦44518\add* worked on the¦44521 courtyard¦44521. For¦44522 the¦44524 south¦44524 side¦44522, the¦44526 courtyard curtains¦44526 were¦44528 fifty metres of twisted¦44529 finely-spun linen¦44528
\v 10 with their¦44533 twenty¦44534 \add bronze\add* pillars and¦44535 their¦44535 bases¦44535. The¦44538 hooks¦44538 on the¦44539 pillars¦44539 and¦44540 their¦44540 rings¦44540 were¦44541 made of silver¦44541.
\v 11 On the¦44544 north¦44544 side¦44543, there were¦44548 fifty metres of¦44549 curtains with their¦44549 twenty¦44550 bronze¦44551 pillars¦44553 and bases¦44549, and their¦44554 silver¦44555 hooks¦44552 and rings¦44554.
\v 12 On the¦44557 west¦44559 side¦44557, there were twenty-five metres of¦44557 curtains¦44560 with their¦44563 ten¦44564 pillars and¦44565 bases¦44565, and their¦44565 silver¦44570 hooks¦44567 and¦44569 rings¦44569,
\v 13 and¦44572 \add another\add* twenty-five metres on the¦44572 east side¦44572.
\v 14 The curtains¦44578 for \add one\add* side¦44585 \add of the entrance\add* were¦44587 7.5m long with their three¦44587 pillars¦44586 and¦44588 their¦44588 bases¦44588.
\v 15 On the \add ≈other\add* side¦44591, opposite the¦44596 courtyard¦44596 entrance¦44595, the curtains¦44597 were¦44598 7.5m long with their¦44601 three¦44602 pillars¦44601 and¦44603 their¦44603 bases¦44603.
\v 16 All¦44606 of¦44606 the¦44609 courtyard¦44609 curtains¦44608 were¦44611 made with twisted¦44612 finely-spun linen¦44611.
\v 17 The¦44614 bases¦44614 for¦44615 the pillars¦44615 were¦44616 bronze¦44616, \add ≈but\add* the¦44617 hooks¦44617 on them and¦44619 their¦44619 rings were¦44620 silver. All¦44627 of¦44627 the¦44629 courtyard¦44629 pillars had decorative silver caps fitted to their¦44622 tops¦44622.
\v 18 The¦44631 curtain for the¦44632 courtyard gate¦44632 was done by an embroiderer. It was made¦44634 from twisted¦44641 finely-spun linen¦44640 \add embroidered\add* with blue, purple¦44637, and¦44638 scarlet yard. The¦44644 curtain was¦44647 ten metres¦44648 long¦44644 and¦44645 2.5m high¦44645, just like¦44649 the¦44650 other courtyard curtains¦44650
\v 19 with its four bronze¦44657 pillars¦44653 and their bases¦44655 and their¦44655 silver hooks¦44658 and¦44660 rings¦44662, and¦44662 with silver¦44663 caps.
\v 20 All¦44665 the¦44667 tent¦44667 pegs¦44667 for¦44668 the \add ≈sacred¦44668 tent¦44668\add* and¦44669 for¦44669 around¦44670 the courtyard¦44669 were¦44671 made with bronze¦44671.
\s1 List of metals used
