\p
\v 21 These¦44674 are¦44675 the records \add from making\add* the \add ≈sacred tent\add* (where the \add stone\add* \add #transcripts¦44678\add* were kept). They were recorded¦44680 by the Levites¦44686 according to Mosheh's¦44684 instructions \add and supervised by\add* Ithamar¦44688 (a son¦44689 of¦44689 Aharon¦44691 the¦44692 priest¦44692).
\p
\v 22 Bezalel¦44694 (son¦44695 of¦44695 Uri¦44697 son¦44698 of¦44698 Hur¦44700, from the¦44701 tribe¦44701 of Judah¦44702) made¦44703 everything that¦44707 Yahweh¦44710 had¦44709 instructed¦44709 Mosheh¦44713 \add <to make\add*.
\v 23 Oholiab¦44716 (son¦44717 of¦44717 Ahisamak, from the¦44720 tribe¦44720 of Dan¦44722) worked with him—he was an¦44723 engraver¦44723 and¦44724 a¦44724 designer¦44724 and an embroiderer in blue, purple¦44727, and¦44728 scarlet, and¦44730 in¦44730 fine linen¦44730.
\p
\v 24 The¦44735 gold¦44735 that¦44736 they used¦44736 for¦44737 the¦44739 construction of¦44739 the¦44740 sacred¦44740 tent was measured at 965kg. This was the¦44743 gold¦44743 from the¦44744 wave offering and was weighed using the official standard weights.
\v 25 The¦44755 silver¦44755 contributed by the¦44757 people¦44757 was¦44758 measured at 3,420kg \add also\add* using the official weights.\x + \xo 38:25-26: \xt Exo 30:11-16.\x*
\v 26 \add During the census,\add* every¦44775 male who¦44776 was twenty¦44781 years¦44782 old or older paid a 5g silver coin\x + \xo 38:26: \xt Mat 17:24.\x*—a total of¦44788 603,550 men.
\v 27 They'd used 3,400kg of silver¦44797 to¦44798 make the¦44800 bases¦44800 \add under the pillars that supported\add* the¦44801 sacred¦44801 tent's curtains¦44804 (34kg for each of one¦44807 hundred¦44807 bases¦44810)
\v 28 and¦44812 the¦44814 other twenty kilograms were used for the¦44816 hooks¦44820 for¦44821 the pillars¦44821 and¦44822 for the caps on the tops¦44823 of¦44823 them¦44825.
\v 29 The¦44827 bronze¦44827 from the¦44828 wave offering came to 2,400kg
\v 30 and¦44837 it¦44837 was used to make¦44837 the¦44841 bases¦44841 \add for the pillars\add* at the¦44843 tent¦44843 entrance¦44842 and¦44845 for the¦44846 altar¦44846 and¦44848 its grating¦44850 and¦44855 all¦44856 the¦44858 utensils¦44858,
\v 31 and¦44861 for the¦44863 bases¦44863 \add for the posts\add* for \add the curtains\add* around the¦44864 courtyard¦44864 and¦44866 at the entrance¦44869, and¦44871 for the¦44874 tent¦44874 pegs¦44874 for the¦44875 \add ≈main structure\add* and¦44876 around the¦44881 courtyard¦44881.
\c 39
\s1 Making the priests' uniforms
