\r (Exo. 28:1-14)
\p
\v 1 They used the blue, purple¦44887, and¦44888 scarlet¦44888 \add cloth\add* to make the¦44889 \add ≈sacred\add* clothes¦44891 to¦44894 be used in¦44895 the sacred tent. They¦44896 made¦44896 Aharon's¦44902 clothes just¦44903 as¦44903 Yahweh¦44905 had¦44904 instructed¦44904 Mosheh¦44908.
\s2 The sacred apron
\rem /s1 The Ephod; Making the Ephod
\p
\v 2 \add @Bezalel¦44911\add* made¦44911 the¦44914 sacred apron¦44914 from twisted¦44921 finely-spun linen¦44920 \add embroidered with\add* gold¦44915 \add wire\add*, and¦44917 blue, purple¦44917, and¦44918 scarlet yarn.
\v 3 They¦44923 hammered¦44923 thin¦44926 sheets of¦44926 gold¦44927 and¦44928 he¦44928 cut¦44928 them¦44928 into \add #thread¦44929\add* of wire for¦44930 a¦44941 skillful¦44941 craftsman to \add ≈embroider\add* into¦44931 the¦44939 fine¦44939 linen¦44939 along with the blue, purple¦44934, and¦44935 scarlet yarn.
\v 4 They¦44944 made¦44944 joined shoulder pieces for it¦44946—joined¦44947 on¦44948 two¦44950 corners
\v 5 and¦44955 the¦44955 skillfully woven waistband¦44955 which¦44957 is attached to the apron was made of the same material of twisted¦44968 finely-spun linen¦44967, and had similar¦44961 embroidery using gold¦44962 \add wire\add*, and¦44964 blue, purple¦44964, and¦44965 scarlet yarn, just¦44969 as¦44969 Yahweh¦44971 had¦44970 instructed¦44970 Mosheh¦44974.
\v 6 They¦44976 cut \add two\add* onyx¦44980 stones¦44979 and mounted¦44982 them in decorative gold¦44983 settings¦44982. The¦44989 names¦44989 of¦44989 the¦44990 \add twelve\add* sons¦44990 of¦44990 Yisra'el¦44991 were engraved on \add them\add* similar to how a signet ring is engraved,
\v 7 and¦44993 he¦44993 put¦44993 them¦44994 on¦44995 the¦44996 shoulder pieces of¦44996 the¦44997 sacred apron¦44997 as stones¦44998 of¦44998 reminder¦44999 for¦45000 the¦45000 sons¦45000 of¦45000 Yisra'el¦45001, as¦45002 Yahweh¦45004 had¦45003 instructed¦45003 Mosheh¦45007.
\s1 Making the sacred pouch
