\r (Exo. 28:15-30)
\p
\v 8 Then¦45010 he¦45010 made¦45010 the¦45013 \add sacred\add* chest pouch which took the¦45014 work¦45014 of¦45014 a¦45015 skilled¦45015 craftsman like¦45016 making the¦45016 sacred apron. It too was made¦45016 of¦45016 twisted¦45024 finely-spun linen¦45023 and embroidered with gold¦45018 \add wire\add*, and¦45020 blue, purple¦45020, and¦45021 scarlet yarn.
\v 9 When the material was¦45027 folded¦45028 over double¦45028, it made¦45029 a square¦45026 pouch that was¦45033 23cm long¦45034 and¦45035 23cm wide¦45036,
\v 10 and¦45039 they¦45039 attached four¦45042 rows¦45043 of¦45043 gemstones¦45044 onto the front. The first row¦45045 had a¦45046 \add red\add* ruby¦45046, a¦45047 \add yellow\add* topaz¦45047, and¦45048 a¦45048 \add red\add* garnet.
\v 11 The¦45053 second¦45053 row¦45052 had a¦45054 \add green\add* emerald¦45056, a¦45055 \add blue\add* sapphire¦45055, and a diamond.
\v 12 The¦45059 third¦45059 row¦45058 had a¦45060 \add red\add* jacinth¦45060, a \add white\add* agate¦45061, and¦45062 a \add purple\add* amethyst¦45062.
\v 13 The¦45065 fourth¦45065 row¦45064 had a¦45066 \add yellow\add* beryl, an¦45067 onyx¦45067, and¦45068 a¦45068 \add green\add* jasper¦45068. \add @All¦45069 the¦45069 stones¦45069\add* were¦45069 mounted¦45070 in decorative gold¦45071 settings¦45072.
\v 14 The¦45074 gemstones were¦45075 engraved with the¦45077 names¦45077 of¦45077 the¦45078 twelve sons¦45078 of¦45078 Yisra'el¦45080 similar to how a¦45088 signet ring is engraved, and they¦45081 represented the¦45087 twelve tribes¦45095.
\v 15 They¦45097 \add attached two\add* twisted¦45102 chains¦45101 of¦45101 pure¦45106 gold¦45105 crafted like a cord onto the pouch,
\v 16 and¦45108 made¦45108 two¦45109 decorative gold settings¦45110 and¦45112 two¦45112 gold rings, and attached them to the \add ≈upper corners\add* of the sacred pouch.
\v 17 They¦45126 attached one \add #end¦45136\add* of¦45127 each gold¦45129 chain to one of¦45132 the¦45133 rings¦45133 on¦45134 the¦45136 \add ≈top corner\add* of¦45136 the¦45137 pouch,
\v 18 and¦45139 they attached the other end¦45141 of¦45141 each chain to the¦45142 two¦45142 decorative settings¦45148 that enclose the¦45143 stones. Then they¦45144 put¦45144 those on¦45145 the¦45147 front¦45156 side of¦45147 the¦45152 shoulder straps of¦45152 the¦45153 sacred apron¦45153.
\v 19 Then¦45159 they¦45159 made¦45159 two¦45160 \add more\add* gold¦45162 rings¦45161 and¦45163 attached them¦45163 to the \add ≈lower corners\add* of the sacred pouch on¦45169 the inside¦45177 \add #edges¦45171\add* next to¦45177 the¦45177 sacred apron.
\v 20 They¦45179 made¦45179 two¦45180 more gold¦45182 rings¦45181 and¦45183 attached them¦45183 to the¦45186 lower¦45189 part of¦45186 the¦45187 front¦45190 of¦45187 the¦45188 shoulder straps near¦45192 where the¦45190 shoulder straps join¦45193 with the sacred apron just above¦45194 the¦45195 waistband¦45195.
\v 21 They¦45198 tied¦45198 the¦45201 rings¦45202 on the sacred pouch to¦45203 the¦45205 rings¦45205 on the¦45206 sacred apron¦45206 with¦45207 a¦45207 blue cord¦45207, so that the sacred pouch was¦45209 above the¦45212 waistband¦45212 and¦45214 would not¦45214 come loose from¦45218 the¦45219 apron¦45219. They did these things exactly as¦45220 Yahweh¦45222 had¦45221 instructed¦45221 Mosheh¦45225 \add <to do\add*.
\s1 Making the other clothes
\rem /s1 Additional Clothing for the Priests; Other Priestly Garments; Making the Other Priestly Garments
\r (Exo. 28:31-43)
\p
\v 22 \add @Bezalel¦45227\add* had a¦45233 weaver¦45233 make¦45227 the¦45230 robe¦45230 \add that would be worn under\add* the¦45231 sacred apron¦45231 entirely¦45234 from blue \add material\add*.
\v 23 It opened¦45237 down the¦45240 middle¦45240 like¦45241 other clothes and had a¦45242 border¦45243 around¦45245 this opening so that it¦45247 wouldn't tear¦45247,
\v 24 and¦45249 the bottom hem had \add decorative\add* pomegranates¦45254 on it that were made¦45249 from blue, purple¦45256, and¦45257 scarlet yarn.
\v 25 They¦45261 \add also\add* made¦45261 \add small\add* bells¦45262 from pure¦45264 gold¦45263 and¦45265 attached them between the¦45270 pomegranates¦45270 around¦45275 the¦45273 bottom of¦45273 the¦45274 robe¦45274,
\v 26 so¦45280 it alternated between a¦45281 bell¦45281 and¦45282 a¦45282 pomegranate¦45282 going around¦45287 the hem, just¦45289 as¦45289 Yahweh¦45291 had¦45290 instructed¦45290 Mosheh¦45294.
\p
\v 27 A¦45303 weaver¦45303 made¦45297 tunics¦45300 for¦45304 Aaron¦45304 and¦45305 his¦45305 sons¦45305 from fine¦45301 linen¦45301,
\v 28 along with the¦45308 turban¦45308 and¦45310 caps from fine¦45314 linen¦45314, the¦45317 underwear¦45317 made from twisted¦45320 finely-spun linen,
\v 29 and¦45322 the¦45324 waistband¦45324 from fine¦45325 linen¦45325 with blue, purple¦45328, and¦45329 scarlet embroidery, just¦45333 as¦45333 Yahweh¦45335 had¦45334 instructed¦45334 Mosheh¦45338.
\p
\v 30 They¦45341 made¦45341 a \add decorative\add* plate¦45344 (to represent a holy crown¦45345) from pure¦45347 gold¦45348 and¦45350 they¦45350 engraved¦45353 ‘Dedicated to¦45356 Yahweh¦45356’ on¦45351 it¦45351 (like you'd do for a¦45354 signet ring).
\v 31 They¦45358 put¦45358 a¦45360 blue cord¦45360 on it to attach it to the front of¦45360 the¦45365 turban¦45365, just¦45367 as¦45367 Yahweh¦45369 had¦45368 instructed¦45368 Mosheh¦45372.
\s1 Mosheh inspects the finished components
