\v 38 the¦45475 gold¦45475 \add incense\add* altar¦45474, the¦45478 anointing¦45478 oil¦45477 and¦45479 the¦45480 fragrant¦45481 incense¦45480, and¦45482 the¦45483 curtain for the¦45485 tent¦45485 entrance¦45484,
\v 39 the¦45489 \add large\add* bronze altar¦45489 with its grating¦45493, its¦45500 poles¦45500, and¦45501 all¦45503 its¦45505 utensils¦45505, the¦45508 washbasin¦45508 with its¦45511 base¦45511,
\v 40 the¦45514 courtyard curtains¦45514 with their pillars¦45518 and¦45519 bases¦45521, the courtyard gate¦45525 curtain, \add all the\add* ropes¦45529 and¦45530 tent¦45530 pegs¦45530 and¦45531 all¦45532 the¦45534 items¦45534 to service¦45535 the¦45536 residence¦45536 as the¦45537 tent¦45537 of¦45537 meeting¦45538,
\v 41 and the¦45542 finely-woven clothes¦45542 for serving¦45544 in¦45545 the holy place¦45545, the \add ≈sacred¦45549\add* clothes for¦45550 Aharon¦45550 the¦45551 priest¦45551, and¦45552 the¦45554 clothes¦45554 for his¦45555 sons¦45555 to¦45556 \add serve as\add* priests¦45556.
\p
\v 42 The¦45568 Israelis¦45568 had done¦45567 all¦45571 the¦45573 work¦45573 just as Yahweh¦45562 had¦45561 instructed¦45561 Mosheh¦45565.
\v 43 Mosheh¦45576 \add ≈inspected\add* all¦45579 the¦45581 work¦45581, and¦45582 wow¦45582, they¦45583 had¦45583 done¦45583 it¦45584 just¦45585 as¦45585 Yahweh¦45587 had¦45589 instructed¦45586 \add <them\add*, and¦45590 Mosheh¦45592 blessed¦45590 them¦45591.
\c 40
\s1 Erecting the sacred tent
\rem /s1 Setting Up the Tabernacle; The Tabernacle Erected and Its Equipment Installed; The Tabernacle Completed; Setting Up and Dedicating the Tent of the Lord's Presence
\p
\v 1 Then¦45595 Yahweh¦45596 told¦45595 Mosheh¦45599,
\v 2 “On¦45602 the first day of the first month¦45607, you¦45608 should set¦45608 up¦45608 the tent¦45612 \add ≈where we'll meet¦45613\add*.
\v 3 Put¦45615 the¦45618 box¦45618 for the¦45619 transcript¦45619 slabs in its place and¦45620 \add hang\add* the¦45626 curtain¦45626 to screen¦45620 it \add from sight\add*.
\v 4 Then¦45628 bring¦45628 in the¦45631 \add bread\add* table¦45631 and¦45632 arrange¦45632 its¦45635 utensils, and¦45636 bring¦45636 in the¦45639 lampstand¦45639 and¦45640 set up¦45640 the lamps¦45643,
\v 5 and¦45645 put¦45654 the¦45649 gold¦45649 incense¦45650 altar¦45648 in¦45651 front¦45651 of¦45651 the¦45652 \add sacred\add* box¦45652 and¦45654 set¦45654 up the¦45658 entrance¦45658 curtain for the tent¦45659.
\v 6 Put the¦45663 altar¦45663 for burning¦45664 sacrifices¦45664 in¦45665 front¦45665 of¦45665 the¦45666 entrance¦45666 to the¦45667 \add ≈sacred¦45667 tent¦45667\add* \add ≈where we'll meet¦45670\add*.
\v 7 Put¦45672 the¦45675 washbasin¦45675 between¦45676 the¦45678 \add sacred\add* tent¦45678 and¦45680 that altar¦45681, and¦45682 fill it with water¦45684.
\v 8 \add ≈Set-up the¦45689 curtains around¦45690 the outside to make the courtyard, and¦45691 also¦45691 set¦45691 up the courtyard's¦45696 entrance¦45695 curtain\add*.
\p
\v 9 Then¦45698 take¦45698 the¦45702 \add sacred\add* anointing¦45702 oil¦45701 and¦45703 \add ≈smear\add* it on the¦45706 \add ≈sacred¦45706 tent¦45706\add* and¦45707 everything that's¦45711 in¦45713 it, then \add ≈none of those things¦45722 should be touched by others\add*—it¦45721 will \add all\add* be¦45721 sacred¦45722.
\v 10 \add ≈Also¦45724\add* anoint¦45724 the¦45727 altar¦45727 for burnt¦45728 \add #offerings¦45728\add* and¦45729 all¦45731 its¦45733 utensils¦45733. After that, the¦45737 altar¦45737 \add ≈shouldn't be touched by others\add*—it¦45738 will be¦45738 \em very\em* \add ≈sacred¦45740\add*.
\v 11 Anoint¦45743 the¦45746 washbasin¦45746 and¦45747 its¦45749 base¦45749, and¦45750 then \add ≈prohibit others from using\add* it¦45751.
\p
\v 12 \add ≈Now\add* bring¦45753 Aharon¦45756 and¦45757 his¦45759 sons¦45759 to¦45760 the¦45762 entrance¦45762 of¦45762 the¦45763 \add sacred\add* tent¦45763 and¦45765 wash¦45765 them¦45766 with¦45767 water¦45767.
\v 13 Then¦45769 put the¦45774 \add ≈sacred\add* garments¦45774 on Aharon¦45772 and¦45776 anoint¦45776 him¦45777 and¦45778 make him¦45779 sacred, so¦45780 he¦45780 can \add now\add* serve¦45780 as¦45780 a¦45780 priest¦45780 to¦45781 me¦45781.
\v 14 \add ≈Also¦45783\add* bring¦45786 his¦45785 sons¦45785 and¦45787 dress¦45787 them¦45788 in tunics¦45789
\v 15 and¦45791 anoint¦45791 them¦45792 like¦45793 you¦45794 anointed¦45794 their¦45797 father¦45797, and¦45798 they¦45798 will¦45798 serve¦45798 as¦45798 priests¦45798 to¦45799 me¦45799. Their¦45803 anointing¦45803 will¦45800 cause them to¦45801 be¦45801 a¦45804 priesthood¦45804 forever¦45805 throughout their¦45806 generations¦45806.”
\p
\v 16 \add ≈So¦45808\add* Mosheh¦45809 did¦45808 \add everything\add* that¦45811 Yahweh¦45813 had¦45812 instructed¦45812 him¦45814 \add <to do\add*.
\v 17 It¦45819 was¦45819 the¦45821 first¦45821 day¦45824 of¦45825 the first month¦45825 of \add &their\add* second year¦45822 when¦45819 they set¦45826 up¦45826 the¦45827 \add ≈sacred¦45827 tent¦45827\add*.
\v 18 Mosheh¦45830 set¦45829 up¦45829 the¦45833 residence¦45833 by setting out its¦45837 bases¦45837 and¦45838 standing up the frames¦45841 with their bars¦45845, and¦45846 the pillars¦45849.
\v 19 He¦45851 spread¦45851 the¦45854 \add ≈two tarpaulin layers\add* over¦45855 the tent¦45862 just¦45865 as¦45865 Yahweh¦45867 had¦45866 instructed¦45866 \add *him¦45870\add*.
\v 20 Then¦45873 he¦45873 took¦45873 the¦45877 \add two stone slabs with the\add* transcript¦45877 and put \add #them\add* into¦45878 the¦45880 box¦45880. He¦45881 put¦45881 the¦45884 poles¦45884 \add into the rings\add* on¦45885 the¦45887 box¦45887 and¦45888 fitted the¦45891 atonement¦45891 platform on¦45892 the top of the¦45894 box¦45894 \add as a lid\add*,
\v 21 and¦45897 brought¦45897 the¦45900 box¦45900 into¦45901 the¦45903 residence¦45903. He¦45904 set up the¦45906 curtain¦45906 to conceal the¦45910 box¦45910 with the¦45911 transcript¦45911, just¦45912 as¦45912 Yahweh¦45914 had¦45913 instructed¦45913 \add *him¦45917\add*.
\p
\v 22 He¦45920 put the¦45923 table¦45923 into¦45924 the¦45924 \add ≈sacred tent¦45924\add* on¦45926 the¦45927 north¦45929 side¦45927 of¦45927 the¦45928 residence¦45928, outside¦45930 the curtain¦45931,
\v 23 and¦45933 arranged¦45933 the bread¦45936 on¦45934 it \add ≈to display it to\add* Yahweh¦45938, just¦45939 as¦45939 Yahweh¦45941 had¦45940 instructed¦45940 \add *him¦45944\add*.
\v 24 He¦45947 put¦45947 the¦45950 lampstand¦45950 inside the¦45951 \add ≈sacred tent¦45951\add* across from the¦45954 table¦45954, on¦45955 the¦45956 south¦45958 side¦45956 of¦45956 the¦45957 residence¦45957,
\v 25 and¦45960 he¦45960 placed the¦45961 lamps¦45961 on it \add ≈in¦45962 Yahweh's¦45963 presence¦45962\add*, just¦45964 as¦45964 Yahweh¦45966 had¦45965 instructed¦45965 \add *him¦45969\add*.
\v 26 Then¦45972 he¦45972 put¦45972 the¦45976 gold¦45976 \add incense\add* altar¦45975 inside the¦45977 \add sacred\add* tent¦45977 in¦45979 front¦45979 of¦45979 the¦45980 curtain¦45980 \add that screened the sacred box from view\add*,
\v 27 and¦45982 burnt¦45982 some fragrant¦45985 incense¦45984 on¦45983 it¦45983, just¦45986 as¦45986 Yahweh¦45988 had¦45987 instructed¦45987 \add *him¦45991\add*,
\v 28 then¦45994 he¦45994 hung the¦45997 curtain at the¦45998 tent¦45999 entrance¦45998.
\v 29 He¦46004 put¦46004 the¦46002 altar¦46002 for burning¦46003 sacrifices¦46003 at the¦46005 gate of¦46005 the¦46006 \add ≈sacred¦46006 tent¦46006\add* and¦46010 offered the¦46014 burnt¦46014 offering¦46014 and¦46015 the¦46017 grain¦46017 offering¦46017 up¦46004 on¦46011 it¦46011, just¦46018 as¦46018 Yahweh¦46020 had¦46019 instructed¦46019 \add *him¦46023\add*.
\v 30 Then¦46026 he¦46026 placed the¦46029 washbasin¦46029 between¦46030 the¦46032 tent¦46032 and¦46034 the¦46035 altar¦46035, and¦46036 filled it¦46036 with water¦46038
\v 31 \add ≈so¦46041 that\add* Mosheh¦46043, and¦46044 Aharon¦46044 and¦46045 his¦46045 sons¦46045, could wash¦46041 their¦46048 hands¦46048 and¦46049 feet¦46051 from it.
\v 32 Whenever¦46053 they went into¦46054 the¦46056 \add sacred\add* tent¦46056 or whenever¦46058 they¦46058 went near¦46058 the¦46061 altar¦46061, \add first\add* they¦46062 would wash¦46062 themselves, just¦46063 as¦46063 Yahweh¦46065 had¦46064 commanded¦46064 Moses¦46068.
\v 33 He¦46071 erected¦46071 the¦46074 courtyard¦46074 \add curtains\add* around¦46075 the residence¦46076 and¦46077 the altar¦46077, and¦46078 he¦46078 set up the courtyard gate¦46082 curtain. And¦46084 \add so\add* Mosheh¦46085 finished¦46084 the¦46088 work¦46088.
\s1 Yahweh's splendour fills the tent
\rem /s1 The Cloud and the Glory; The Glory of the Lord; The Lord's Glory Fills the Tabernacle; The Cloud over the Tent of the Lord's Presence
\r (Num. 9:15-23)
\p
\v 34 Then¦46091 a cloud¦46092 covered¦46091 the¦46095 \add ≈sacred tent¦46095\add* and¦46097 Yahweh's¦46098 \add ≈power and bright light\add* filled¦46099 the¦46102 residence¦46102\x + \xo 40:34: \xt 1Ki 8:10-11; Isa 6:4; Eze 43:4-5; Rev 15:8.\x*
\v 35 and¦46104 Mosheh¦46107 was¦46106 unable to¦46108 enter the¦46111 tent¦46111 because¦46113 the¦46117 cloud¦46117 had¦46115 settled¦46115 on¦46116 it¦46116 and¦46118 Yahweh's¦46119 splendour¦46118 had¦46120 filled¦46120 the¦46123 residence¦46123.
\v 36 \add From then onwards,\add* whenever¦46125 the¦46126 cloud¦46126 went up¦46125 from¦46127 over the¦46128 residence¦46128, the¦46130 Israelis¦46130 would \add pack their camp and\add* set¦46129 out on their¦46133 travels,
\v 37 but¦46135 while the¦46139 cloud¦46139 remained, they¦46141 would stay in that place¦46141 until¦46142 the¦46144 cloud lifted¦46145.
\v 38 Yahweh's¦46149 cloud¦46148 would be¦46150 there during the¦46152 day¦46153 \add ≈but¦46154\add* it would become fire¦46154 at night¦46156, and so the Israelis¦46163 \add ≈could always see it\add*.
